Package: BayesianStatisticalIntervalsCalculator
Title: Credible, Prediction and Tolerance Intervals from MCMC Output
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R:
    c(person("Ekin", "Ören", , "ekin.oren.3@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
      person("Sebastian", "Schmitz", role = "aut"),
      person("Sanofi", role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: Computes and visualizes credible intervals, prediction intervals
    and tolerance intervals, together with posterior predictive
    distributions, from Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) draws of a Bayesian
    linear mixed model. Users choose the fixed effects, variance components
    and optional covariates that define the model, and results can be
    back-transformed from the log scale. Two-sided tolerance intervals with
    asymmetric limits can be obtained with the Krishnamoorthy approach, and
    reducible-uncertainty ratios contrast the tolerance and prediction
    bounds relative to the median. An interactive 'shiny' application is
    included.
